uestion-7dc41e95-539c-50b9-8fb0-b63764e8684c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275978"] ["question-7dc41e95-539c-50b9-8fb0-b63764e8684c" :question/problem "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(x,w)={(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}-4{x}^{T}w\n$$\n\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find ${∇}_{w}f.$ You may assume that $w$ has no zero components."] ["question-7dc41e95-539c-50b9-8fb0-b63764e8684c" :question/worked-solution "Using the results\n\n$$\n{∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})=\\text{sign}(w),\\,{∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w)=x,\n$$\n\n we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}-4{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})-{∇}_{w}(4{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})-4\\cdot {∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})-4\\cdot x \\\\  & =3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-4\\cdot x \\\\  & =3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-7dc41e95-539c-50b9-8fb0-b63764e8684c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-e5042304-8241-5082-82cb-26bee7d6fc07" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5042304-8241-5082-82cb-26bee7d6fc07"] ["answer-ca5a0474-5015-51cb-829b-d6477c15697d" :answer/id #uuid "ca5a0474-5015-51cb-829b-d6477c15697d"] ["answer-ca5a0474-5015-51cb-829b-d6477c15697d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ca5a0474-5015-51cb-829b-d6477c15697d" :answer/value "(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-4x"] ["answer-e7e63be3-9e49-5062-b7d5-c7b2c1a4ae27" :answer/id #uuid "e7e63be3-9e49-5062-b7d5-c7b2c1a4ae27"] ["answer-e7e63be3-9e49-5062-b7d5-c7b2c1a4ae27" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e7e63be3-9e49-5062-b7d5-c7b2c1a4ae27" :answer/value "3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-4w"] ["answer-bd827637-7b44-5716-8016-3b379e1ce6d6" :answer/id #uuid "bd827637-7b44-5716-8016-3b379e1ce6d6"] ["answer-bd827637-7b44-5716-8016-3b379e1ce6d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bd827637-7b44-5716-8016-3b379e1ce6d6" :answer/value "3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-4x"] ["answer-9fb156c9-d84f-5baa-add4-3f456c7cf40a